    {
      "id": "yeats-collected-poems-s0331-p00688",
      "source_en": "Fled foam underneath us, and round us, a wandering and\nmilky smoke,\nHigh as the saddle-girth, covering away from our glances the\ntide;\nAnd those that fled, and that followed, from the foam-pale\ndistance broke;\nThe immortal desire of Immortals we saw in their faces, and\nsighed.",
